The clerk types on his computer.
He gives me the SIM card.
"Here is your new number," he says.
He gives me a slip of paper.
I take my phone.
I put the SIM card into my phone.
"I am checking the number," I say.
I read the number aloud:
"Zero one seven six, one two three four five six seven eight."
"Is that correct?" I ask.
"Yes, that is correct," the clerk says.
"That is your number."
The mobile phone works.
I have a German number now.
I write a message right away.
I write to Jonas from the office.
"Hello Jonas, Maya here," I type.
"I have a new number now."
Now the office has my number.
